  "id": "COMPOUND:17155 - PROTEIN:5839",
  "verbalization": "Undecanol is implicated in the relationship with U251 through a multi-step mechanistic pathway. The evidence suggests that Undecanol acts as a target for Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is subsequently targeted by a complex compound, [(1S,2S,6R,7R,9R,10S,11S,12R,14S)-11-hydroxy-14-methyl-5-methylidene-4-oxospiro[3,13-dioxatetracyclo[8.4.0.02,6.012,14]tetradecane-9,2'-oxirane]-7-yl] (E)-4-hydroxy-2-methylbut-2-enoate. This compound, in turn, targets U251, indicating a potential biological pathway involving phosphatase inhibition. Additionally, Undecanol is also shown to target Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is also targeted by sec-Butyl acetate, (-), further reinforcing the role of this phosphatase in the pathway. The evidence suggests that Undecanol may modulate the activity of this phosphatase, potentially influencing U251 through a mechanism involving phosphatase inhibition. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Undecanol in modulating the activity of the phosphatase, which in turn may affect U251. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple targets and the consistent involvement of the phosphatase in the pathway.",
